// Global settings for mai (Multi-AI CLI)
// Edit review and plan prompts and other global settings here
{
  // Prompt sent to each AI reviewer tool
  "review_prompt": "Review changes in this branch against {{base_branch}}.\n\nTo see only the PR changes (excluding unrelated commits on {{base_branch}}), use:\n  git diff $(git merge-base origin/{{base_branch}} HEAD)..HEAD\n\nA pre-computed diff of these changes is available in CHANGES.diff.\n\nOnce done with the review, write findings to REVIEW.md\n\nMarkdown formatting: write each paragraph as a single line. Do not hard-wrap lines at a fixed column width (e.g. 80 characters).",

  // Template for the meta reviewer prompt
  // {{review_locations}} is replaced with the list of REVIEW.md file paths at runtime
  "meta_prompt_template": "Your task is to review the code reviews made by other AI tools. You will find the review markdown files from these locations:\n{{review_locations}}\n\nPlease wait for the REVIEW.md files to appear, then read all of the reviews, and create a comprehensive summary of the review results. You can investigate the repo and review results if needed. Use sub-agents if needed.\n\nOnce you are done, create two files:\n1. REVIEW_SUMMARY.md — consolidated findings including which AI tool made each observation\n2. REVIEW_SUMMARY_UNIFIED.md — unified review without any app-specific attribution, presenting findings as a single cohesive review\n\nMarkdown formatting: write each paragraph as a single line. Do not hard-wrap lines at a fixed column width (e.g. 80 characters).",

  // Prompt sent to each AI planner tool
  "plan_prompt": "You are tasked with creating a detailed implementation plan for a feature or change in this codebase.\n\n## Your Process\n\n1. **Explore the codebase first**: Read relevant files, trace code paths, and understand existing patterns before writing anything. Check docs/, recent commits, and any existing plans. Use the brainstorming skill (/superpowers:brainstorming) if available to explore user intent and requirements.\n\n2. **Create the plan**: Produce a comprehensive, step-by-step implementation plan. Use the writing-plans skill (/superpowers:writing-plans) if available. The plan should include:\n   - Clear problem statement and goals\n   - Architecture decisions with reasoning\n   - Step-by-step implementation tasks (bite-sized, each independently testable)\n   - File paths and specific changes for each task (what to add, modify, or remove)\n   - Dependencies between tasks (what must be done first)\n   - Testing strategy for each task\n   - Edge cases, risks, and open questions\n   - What can be parallelized vs what must be sequential\n\n3. **Write findings to PLAN.md**: Create a PLAN.md file in the worktree root with your complete plan.\n\n## Guidelines\n- Prefer small, incremental changes over large rewrites\n- Follow existing code patterns and conventions in the codebase\n- Consider backward compatibility\n- Flag any decisions that need human input before proceeding\n- Include exact file paths and code snippets where helpful\n- The plan should be executable by another AI agent with no additional context",

  // Template for the meta planner prompt
  // {{plan_locations}} is replaced with the list of PLAN.md file paths at runtime
  "plan_meta_prompt_template": "Your task is to synthesize the implementation plans created by multiple AI tools into a single unified plan. You will find the individual plans from these locations:\n{{plan_locations}}\n\nPlease wait for the PLAN.md files to appear, then read all of the plans thoroughly. You can investigate the repo if needed. Use sub-agents if needed.\n\n## Your Process\n\n1. Read and compare all plans carefully — note areas of agreement and disagreement\n2. Evaluate each plan for correctness, completeness, and feasibility\n3. Identify the best ideas from each plan and resolve conflicts\n\n## Deliverables\n\nCreate two files:\n\n1. **PLAN_SUMMARY.md** — Comparison of all plans:\n   - Which AI tool proposed each approach\n   - Areas of consensus (approaches most planners agree on)\n   - Areas of divergence (with your assessment of which approach is better and why)\n   - Unique insights from individual planners that others missed\n\n2. **PLAN_UNIFIED.md** — The definitive unified implementation plan:\n   - Single coherent task list with no attribution to individual tools\n   - Clear sequencing and dependencies between tasks\n   - Each task bite-sized and independently executable\n   - Testing strategy included\n   - Ready to be executed with /superpowers:executing-plans or /superpowers:subagent-driven-development"
}
